     The aaccll__ffrreeee() call allows the freeing of ACL working space, such as is
     allocated by acl_dup(3), or acl_from_text(3).

IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     FreeBSD's support for POSIX.1e interfaces and features is still under de‐
     velopment at this time.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The aaccll__ffrreeee() function returns the value 0 if successful; otherwise the
     value -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the
     error.

EERRRROORRSS
     If any of the following conditions occur, the aaccll__ffrreeee() function shall
     return -1 and set _e_r_r_n_o to the corresponding value:

     [EINVAL]           The value of the _o_b_j___p argument is invalid.

